FATAL_OBJECTIONS: [
  "evaluation_prosecutor RED — M/G/1 non-preemptive model structurally misrepresents continuous batching (iteration-level decode, preemption/swapping, batched prefill). The head-of-line blocking that drives the 1.4-5.8x p99 ratio may collapse under processor-sharing-like dynamics. This is NOT fully rebutted at L0; it IS explicitly gated by the pre-reg's L1 requirement. Disposition: MANAGEABLE — the RED is grounded but overstated for an L0 that self-declares its model limitations and gates promotion on exactly the real-system validation the prosecutor demands. The controls (C1 oracle, C2 tau-invariance) are informative WITHIN the M/G/1 model and establish the mechanism; the MAGNITUDE is what is model-dependent. Partial rebuttal, not dismissal — L1 must close this gap or the RED stands."
